cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHOTO-CAT in published work, please cite the project and replace the placeholder paper reference when the final paper is available."
title: "PHOTO-CAT: Photometric Contamination Analyzer Tool"
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PHOTO-CAT contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Daddi14/photo-cat"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
abstract: "PHOTO-CAT is a Python package for catalogue-level photometric contamination risk assessment and target screening. It builds a neighbour index from an astronomical catalogue and queries nearby sources that may contaminate selected photometric targets using an aperture-like catalogue flux-ratio model."
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - photometry
  - contamination
  - catalogue
  - Python
